NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1055,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,2,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":9,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0868,"rank":0.1503,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV002502","role":"target","render":{"description":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45349"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV002004","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","place":"Mussel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43322","original":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.955,7.03889]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006902","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43572","original":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV007506","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","place":"Veelerveen","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44134","original":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.05583,7.12778]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Mussel.","Find Barlage on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.0125,7.05556],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Barlage"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3058,"rank":0.6075,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1105,"rank":0.1715,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV011104","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Roosters that crow at nine o'clock in the evening or later predict rain and wind.","place":"Sellingen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"TM 4001","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43504","original":"As de hoanen s oavends om n uur of negen of loater nog kraaien, den kriegn ie gauw regen en wind.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ032601","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A card reader tells a woman that she is going to have a very hard time. Shortly afterwards the woman is widowed and left with nine children. Coffee-ground readers are also often consulted to foretell the future.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22120","original":"Mem hat us by in kaertlizter yn Ljouwert west. Dy hat tsjin mem sein: \"Hwat krije jo in swier jok to dragen, frou. Mar hâld de moed der yn.\"\nMem hat heit al jong forlern. Sy bleau sitten mei njoggen bern. Hja hat it o sa swier hawn.\nDe lju gongen ek wol nei Thomas' Clare, mar dy koe 't sa goed net. Dy seach yn 't kofjedik (anderen vertellen dat ze kaarten gebruikte).","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ011311","role":"omen","render":{"description":"At an empty spot, people often heard hammering in the evening from nine o'clock on. Years later a farm came there.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17750","original":"Yn 'e Surhústermieden by de feart wie in plak, dêr gong it nachts faek op in timmerjen. Njoggen ûre jouns dan bigong it. Altyd klunderen se dêr nachts om. Mar der wie dêrom neat as men der hinne gong.\n\"Hjir komt fêst in hûs\", seinen wy tsjin elkoar.\nIt hat noch jierren duorre, doe is dêr in nij spultsje delset woarn, flak by de brêge.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","9 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":9},"on_success":{"chime":9,"digit":{"value":9,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7036,"rank":0.7241,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VODA_035_14","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The old farmhand is afraid. A young, fearless farmhand offers to take the horses to the meadow and bring them back from now on. One day the young farmhand also sees a burning candle on the gate and two floating ladies. The horses are restless. The farmhand knocks the candle off the gate and the two ladies vanish at once. The horses are calm again. From then on, however, the young farmhand is tormented night after night by the white lady, who wants her light back, and after six weeks he dies of it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"OIRSCHOT095","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The daughters tucked their skirts into trousers and wore a cloth around their hair. People saw white women around the castle and thought they were ghosts. But they were probably the lady of the castle and her daughters.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LAAN004a","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"On the border of Slochteren and Schildwolde they walked up and down an oak avenue in long white robes. They were never seen by day, but they were not afraid. They were in eerie places and in churchyards. They were also always at places where something had happened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ001413","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He murdered his aunt for her money and since then it has been haunted there. All this happens close to the spot where the house of strong Hearke once stood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"LYST293","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Her dress is covered with feathers. Often in the morning some of these little feathers can be seen lying on the road. Her presence seems to have a fatal influence.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"LAAN005","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There was one widde juvver (white lady) whose gown was too long, so everyone tripped over it. A ziever cut it off, and from then on things always went well for him and his family.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"ZEEUW049","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Since then Miss Jenne has not been seen again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"LYST030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In return she must run naked through the church. She does so reluctantly. Later a wit wief (white woman) can be seen on the land she was given. People are convinced that the woman's ghost still haunts it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"LYST265","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The mower flees. The mower's neighbour thinks the man probably saw a poacher or smuggler with a white sheet around him. It might also have been someone who wanted to frighten young girls.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"LYST041","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They are badly frightened because they think it is the ill-omened figure of a wit wief (white lady). Later they see that the figure is not a wit wief but a white goat standing with its legs against the tree, eating the leaves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0311. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c3"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c3"],"stack":["c1","c3"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2246,"rank":0.733,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ009417","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the past witte wieven (white women) were often seen at night in Westerein.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17488","original":"Froeger waerden der wol wite wiven sjoen nachts yn 'e Westerein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1426","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Strange people were said to dress up as a werewolf.","place":"Woudrichem","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125543","original":"In mijn jeugd ging het verhaal van de weerwolf, da 't toen zo was, da vreemde mense zich verkleed hadde. Dan sprake ze van de weerwolf.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ007910","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the lane by Hattum de Vries a wit wijf (white woman) always haunted at night. People did not dare go there at night, because the white woman drove them to the side towards the little lake. Without doing anything themselves, they ended up in the lake.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17053","original":"By Hattum de Vries yn it loantsje spoeke nachts altyd in wyt wiif. De minsken doarsten dêr nachts noait to kommen. Hwant sy waerden dêr stadich troch dat wite wiif oan kant treaun nei de dobbe ta. Sûnder dat se it sels fornamen kommen se yn 'e dobbe torjochte.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"DYKFRIES2187","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the time of Emperor Lothair, many witte wijven (white women) lived in Friesland. These were malicious spirits and ghosts that carried people and children off to their lair. Later these beings were called witte juffers (white ladies), but these were friendly and helpful by nature.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69790","original":"Ten tijde van keizer Lotharius werd men in Friesland veel geplaagd door geesten en spoken. Zij woonden op de spits van een kleinen heuvel in een kunstig hol, dat door geen menschenhanden was gemaakt. Gewoonlijk werden zij witte wijven genoemd. Aangaande hare uiterlijke gedaante wist men niet veel. Nachtelijke wandelaars, veehoeders, vrouwen en kinderen werden dikwijls door deze witte wijven weggevoerd naar hare holen en onderaardsche gangen. Daaruit hoorde men niet zelden zuchten, snikken en kindergeschrei. Zorgvuldig bewaakte men daarom zwangere vrouwen en kinderen, opdat dezen niet door de witte vrouwen zouden worden weggehaald. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Woudrichem belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0901,"rank":0.7966,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ005402","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator's father was once going back from Sânbulten to Zwaagwesteinde at one o'clock at night. In the Zwagerbosch he suddenly saw five women standing there wearing pointed caps and long white skirts. There was not a breath of wind, yet the plumes of the caps waved to and fro. He was frightened to death and went to old Bearn's farm. When they went to look together, the women were gone.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16510","original":"Heit hat us in kear nei de Sânbulten to praten west. Om ien ûre yn 'e nacht gong er werom nei de Westerein ta. Op Sânbulten moest er oer 't spoar en sa kom er troch Sweagerbosk. 't Wie blêdstil en moai sacht waer. Der wie neat dat him forroerde.\nDoe seach heit dêr yn Sweagerbosk ynienen fiif froulju stean, allegear mei in puntmûtse op en lange wite rokken oan. Hoewol it blêdstil waer wie, waeiden de tûfen [fan] de puntmûtsen al mar hinne en wer. Heit wie deabinaud. Hy gong nei âlde Bearn op 't hiem en kloppe dêr op 'e achterdoar. Hy kloppe Bearn der út. Hy fortelde Bearn mei in triljend lûd hwat er sjoen hie. Doe gong Bearn mei him om nei dy froulju to sjen. Mar doe wie der net ien mear. Doe't heit yn 'e Westerein oankom, trille er noch.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ034801","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte juffers (white maidens) haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22700","original":"Us mem biwearde, to Aldegea spoeke it op in smel reedtsje by Jan Japiksma. Dêr wie in boskje mei in gracht der omhinne. Dêr spoeken wite juffers.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a crossroads near Jistrum it was haunted at night. One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12146","original":"Wite juffers\nTe Jistrum, oan 'e noardkant, dêr krúst de Spoekloane de wei dy't fan Jistrum nei de Grinzerstrjitwei rint. Op dat krúspunt doogde it lang net. Dêr gong wol ris in wite gestalte dwers oer de wei, flak foar de minsken lâns. Ik wit noch wol, dat ien fan Durk Jaringa's jonges-se wennen oan 'e grutte strjitwei- de jûnes nei 'De Lindeboom' yn Jistrum west hie - sa hiet de jachtweide fan Jan van der Schors. It hie der tige gesellich west, hy hie in slokje dronke en om in oere of tsien, alven sette er op hûs yn. Hy kaam dêr op dy fjouwersprong en dêr gong dy wite gestalte flak foar him lâns. Hy waard sa kjel, dat hy stode hals oer de kop wer nei Justrum ta en dêr fûn er andergeloks noch lju yn 'e herberch. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ZEEUW047","role":"card","render":{"description":"At night a white woman appears and disappears into a well. After the well is filled in, she no longer appears.","place":"Yerseke","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.D.v.O.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38973","original":"Witte Juffers\nOok te Ierseke verscheen de Witte Vrouw op een stuk grond tusschen Lepel- en Mosselstraat. Later heeft men uit de voorwerpen die daar gevonden zijn, kunnen nagaan dat dit opgehoogde terrein in de oudheid als kerkhof heeft gediend, en vermoedelijk ook een vluchtheuvel was.\nVele omwonenden hebben haar, in het holle van den nacht, gezien. Ze verdween dan altijd in een diepe welput. Na het dichten van de put, kwam de witte vrouw niet weer. Ze had rust gevonden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ063612","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Almelo they have witte wijven (white women) and a beautiful woman haunts the place. I heard that when I was buying horses there.","place":"Soesterberg","prov":"Utr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27090","original":"In Almelo hebben ze witte wiven. En daar spookt ook nog een mooie vrouw om. Ik heb het daar wel eens gehoord toen ik daar peerden kocht.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c6","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c6","word":"three","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"080b20c013cf6858","accepted_hashes":["20e990d55d6120781c7829acbd81b8d0fb8fa9004618bb762dc5bc5cc36a0767","bef1dd43643fd58bd7d8122a7ed370a4b0b20fdf85876aaf5c2b6e8056963844","c3f1f86ebaf1e96bdda16f6ecbf714a83e60234c2183e92e6f8e01e2f0abf2ec","d6ff86e0c0fad0c485483a1a3d187556e7c6f703e053d2c7708e41ebff3069cb"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2964,"rank":0.8826,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ057010","role":"member","render":{"description":"If you meet a werewolf, you must throw him a handkerchief. A werewolf was once courting his girl. Suddenly he wanted her apron and ran off. When he came back a little later, the threads of the apron were still between his teeth. He had torn it apart.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25806","original":"As jo in wjerwolf tomjitte komme, dan matte jo se in bûsdoek tasmite.\nDer wie in wjerwolf, dy kom by in faem. Hy siet by har to frijen. Doe gong hy der ynienen út.\n\"'k Mat dyn skelk even mei ha\", sei er.\nDoe't hy der wer ynkom hongen him de triedden fan 'e skelk ta de mûle út. Dy hied er forskuord.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ052012","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman, wife of a werewolf, is suddenly bitten in her red woollen skirt. As a werewolf, her husband regularly has to bite into something. Red yarn shows in his molars. Werewolves especially like to sink their teeth into red wool.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25177","original":"Der wie in faem, dy troude mei in wjerwolf. Hja hie in read baeijen rôk oan. Hy gong achter har stean en doe biet er hiel bot yn dy rôk. Hy hie de reade triedden fan it guod noch yn 'e kiezzen sitten.\n\"Hast it wol sjoen?\" seinen har âlden tsjin syn frou.\nWjerwolven matte nou en dan bite, dat kinne se net litte. Fral yn read baei meije se graech bite.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ039817","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man asks his sweetheart for a handkerchief and disappears with it. When he returns, red threads from the handkerchief hang between his teeth. He confesses that he is a werewolf who must tear something apart now and then, and had asked for a handkerchief so as not to tear her apart.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23534","original":"Der wienen in feint en in faem, dy wienen togearre út to riden.\nUnderweis lei de feint de swipe del en hy liet it hynder stilstean.\nDe faem sei tsjin 'e feint: \"Hwat silstû?\"\n\"Jow my de bûsdoek\", sei er. Doe joech se him in reade bûsdoek. Dêr gong er mei fuort.\nDoe't er in skoftsje fuort west hie, kom er werom. Doe hied er de reade triedden fan 'e bûsdoek tusken de tosken hingjen.\n\"Hwat hastû dien?\" sei se.\nDoe hied er bikend dat er in wjerwolf wie. Hy moest nou en dan hwat forskuorre. Dêrom hied er om 'e bûsdoek frege, oars hied er har forskuorre matten.\nDoe hat dy faem de forkearing gau út makke.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL001916","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Acquainted with people who can turn into werewolves; a woman sees a werewolf or the devil.","place":"Maurik","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209980","original":"Men wist nog wel mensen te noemen, die de naam hadden te kunnen weerwolven. Wat ze deden, wist men niet.\nDe \"aauwe\" Roel moest de weerwolf of was het \"den duvel\" verdrijven. Zij zag hem komen en schreeuwde 's nachts: \"Daor heddum al weer\" (moet in Ingen gebeurd zijn, de \"aauwe\" Roel was de buurvrouw.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Maurik belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.111,"rank":0.8462,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ071510","role":"door","render":{"description":"A werewolf is a young man who rides a horse. He torments the horse just as a nightmare torments a person. He is one of seven brothers.","place":"Rohel","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28067","original":"In wjerwolf is in manspersoan, - meastal in jongkeardel -, dy't op in hynder rydt. Hy pleaget dat hynder, krekt as in nachtmerje de minsken. 't Is ien fan sawn bruorren. Ik ha wol ien kend, dy wenne yn Warffum.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"TINNEV042","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two men are looking for grass stalks to cut. When they find none, they go home. After they have parted, one of the men suddenly sees a large wolf on his path. The next morning the other man asks him whether he saw the wolf.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22388","original":"29.\nPeter ging op een kier met Dorus mieskes sni'je. Mao zi'j konne de gin vinne en wolle daorum weer op huus aan. De weg liep deur een buske. Dorus vroeg aan Peter offe um nao huus sol brenge. \"Loop nao da galg\", antwore Peter en kroap onder de scheibeum nève de weg hèèr.\n\"Hi'j is ter\", riep Dorus um nao. Ienéns stong d'r een grote wolf op de bosweg. Hi'j wol niet op zied gaon. Daorum drèèje Peter de met een flinken boag umhen. Toe e is umkek zag e niks meer. Umdat Peter geld neudig had ginge de 's marges weer op uut um smele te zuke. Ien Kilder was Dorus al met een groten trop aan 't sni'je. Toe hi'j Peter zag riep tem toe: \"Wasse d'r now, of niet?\".","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c2"},"stack":["c2","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6696,"rank":0.25,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV009505","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At midnight the ghost of a murdered person haunts and blood spatters up at the place of the murder. A boy then does not dare look over his right shoulder.","place":"Stadskanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44586"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV015701","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Late in the evening a man notices that the back door of the cowshed is open and hears rumbling that does not come from the cows. The farmer says that a woman who was murdered there haunts now and then.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45797","original":"Mien voader kon kwoad zain en hef mie door veul van verteld. Hai dainde as jongkerel bie de boer. Op n keer kwam e wat loat in hoes. Dan gung e deur de achterdeure van de dele, umdat andere deurn dicht zatn. As hai dan dele opstapt, heurt hai n geluud, man zug niks. \n“Kou lös”, denkt e. Hai zöcht n schienvat op en gait de baistn bie langs. Man nee heur, alles is rustig. \n Zeker wat verbeeld, zo denkt hai. Nich laank loater overkomp hum t zulfde; weer gestommel op dele en t binnen gain koi-en, dai t doun. \nNon wait hai nich meer, wat e door van denkn mout. Wol wait hai wizze, dat e nooit meer deur de baanderdeure wil. \nAnder dag under t eetn proot hai dr over mit de boer. Dai zeg eerst niks. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ105507","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At night one can sometimes see the white apparition of a murdered woman.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37578","original":"Mem fortelde, hjir yn 'e Pein hat in huzinge stien mei in gracht der by. Dêr is alris in frommeske formoarde woarn. Sûnt seach men dêr nachts in frou yn 't wyt troch de gracht hinne rinnen. Dat wie dat formoarde frommeske.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Groningen a time of day was mentioned: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1965.","That card names a time of day. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"080b20c013cf6858","accepted_hashes":["1039c1cff0d422931688880fcabb6358f73ff7680edb9fc4c8aac159b377a176","1d5952dadae0b945568e6790a63c236e45934f979bd991993c817d51ef18270c","28b7ba6c321501672786f963091d16a188166763aa1a76a4dacbae1dbeffa910","29871823b86551b627a6be2e3f950d103c308ce9ce9a8665f70434aab216338e","9048f57bc282ab9b42508e674d201393d7f61ee121f4f2678eec06a268470fab"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1592,"rank":0.6209,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VRIES006005","role":"member","render":{"description":"Cases of witchcraft and haunting, buying off a bewitchment by paying a doctor who can work magic, black cat in a box bed.","place":"Axel","prov":"Zl.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"J.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209468","original":"ZWARTE KUNST RONDOM ZAAMSLAG.\n\nDaar liep vroeger een padje van 't Turp naar de Groenstrate. \nDaar in de buurte ei moeder vroeger geweund. A moeder in 't schemerdonker langs dà padje liep, stond d 'er wel is een klein sliepsteentje mee een bakje water d 'er onder. En da dieng stong zomaa te draaien, zonder datter iemand ankwam.\nZe zei dà thuus en der broers zeien: \"daa moe je nie meer langs lopen (h)oor!\"\n't Gebeurden ook wè, dat ze swinters de waste (was) op zolder te drogen iengen (hingen) en dan was 't daa boven soms een leven as een oordeel. Toen à ze giengen kiekken zagen ze de kousen gewoon rechtop over de zolder lopen. …","lang":"Zeelandic","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VRIES002602","role":"member","render":{"description":"Poltergeist in the form of a tall man haunts a farm.","place":"Zaamslag","prov":"Zl.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"J.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209242","original":"IN DE SCHUUR VAN SCHELFHOUT. \n\n\"'t Verhaal over \"den ouwen Roose\" ken U misschien nog niet, meneer? \nDat is veel langer geleden, want mijn moeder had het al als kind van haar moeder gehoord.\nRoose, die op deVal woonde, stond in de hele buurt bekend als een vent die je nergens bang mee kon krijgen en dat wou in die dagen rondom de Val wet wat zeggen! Zeker ook, omdat er in de buurt al een paar vreemde dingen gebeurd waren.\nOp een zomernacht gaat Roose, 1e knecht bij boer Schelfhout, die in de Grote Huijssenspolder woonde, een kwartiertje lopen van deVal af, om 2 uur op weg. 't Is oogsttijd en al vroeg moeten de paarden aan 't werk kunnen gaan. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ037017","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) have been seen at a haunted spot.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22990","original":"Oan 'e Akkereed by de Brandsma-wei yn Garyp spoeken wite wiven, seinen se.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VRIES002906","role":"member","render":{"description":"Woman is grabbed by the throat at dusk.","place":"Zaamslag","prov":"Zl.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"J.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209256","original":"'k bin zelf nooit bange gewist, ma kort bie de kreke an Pauwvliet (aan hoofdweg Axel-Zaamslag) bin 'k is bie m 'en kele gegrepen; 't was tussen licht en donker.\nWad of 't gewist is weet ik nie. De politie ei-ter nog na gezocht, ma z 'en niks kunnen vinden.\n\nNoe, meer weet ik nie meer. Misschien datter me later nog wè wat invalt, dad oor je dan nog wè; in bedankt da je gewist ziet!","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Garyp belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1273,"rank":0.375,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST162","role":"top","render":{"description":"In the old days people said you should not walk in the middle of the road after dark, or you ran the risk of being thrown to the side of the road or into the verge. It also happened that people were followed by a dog that kept walking along until they reached home. In wooded areas","place":"Oranjewoud","prov":"Fr.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13413","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ010112","role":"half","render":{"description":"The beast is very big and yellow, and it flaps its ears. It passes right by the man and stays with him for a while. The man thinks it was a plaagbeest (tormenting beast).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST162","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"two fiery eyes would sometimes stare at people. Those eyes were the \"Evil One\", always lying in wait.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333","stain":"two"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ080711","role":"half","render":{"description":"In the middle of the road stood a very big dog that would not let him pass. That was a plaagbeest (a phantom beast that harasses people). The man went back again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0256"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ018108","role":"half","render":{"description":"When the rats ran around, you could hear the money jingle. When the place was later demolished, they found all the money. It was a haunted place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP280","role":"half","render":{"description":"They brought misfortune to anyone who tried to chase them away. Such chained dogs also used to appear in the area around Broekhuizen, Broekhuizenvorst, Blitterswijk, Wanssum, Geysteren, Maashees and Venray. In Blitterswijk it was called the 'patershond' (friar's dog), and people preferred to keep well away from it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ060905","role":"half","render":{"description":"When Schopper, the director of the Wilhelminahoeve, hears this he does not believe it, but he has to admit she is right when they see it themselves too.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The machine stops in mid-sentence. The rest finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0333. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c3","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c3"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c3"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
